 *   **Strengths:** No preprocessing required; handles dynamic particle sets; fast neighbor access via influence-cache; reduced memory reads via slab-cache; interactive frame rates [S1, unofficial].
 *   **Limitations:** Approximation error from LOD (though negligible); high register usage limits occupancy on older GPUs; requires rebuilding octree every frame [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## Background
-The method was presented by Jens Orthmann, Maik Keller, and Andreas Kolb from the University of Siegen, Germany [S1, unofficial]. It builds on data-parallel octrees by Zhou et al. [ZGHG10] and stackless traversal techniques by Popov et al. [PGSS07]. It is designed for ad-hoc visualization of SPH fluid simulations directly after each simulation step [S1, unofficial].
